{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Glenn Cooper (born January 8, 1953) is an American author and physician best known for being an internationally best selling thriller writer.","title":"Glenn Cooper"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His books have been translated into 31 languages and, as of 2014, have sold over six million copies.","title":"Glenn Cooper"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He currently lives in Gilford, New Hampshire.","title":"Glenn Cooper"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Dalbir Singh Jhand known as Punjabi writer Dalbir Chetan was a foremost short-story writer of contemporary Punjabi literature.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He had won awards, both regional and national, and is a widely translated author.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He retired as Indian Air Force officer.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The renowned Punjabi writer Dalbir Chetan (60), whose works were translated into a number of South-East Asian languages, is no more.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Though not a prolific writer, he was the author of four thought-provoking short story books — Rishteyian De Aar Paar, Raat Baraate, Khara Badal and Mehndi Bazaar book's main story Mehndi Bazaar was translated and reviewed in journal South Asian Review.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" His book Mehndi Bazaar was translated into seven South-East Asian languages and selected in Twenty Stories from South Asia.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Many of his stories were translated into Urdu, English, Hindi, Oriya, Telugu and Gujarati languages.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Some of his short stories were telecast on television.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" He also edited an anthology "Asi Javaab Dinde Haan", which won him appreciation.","title":"Dalbir Chetan"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Natalia Ginzburg, (] ; ] ; 14 July 1916 – 7 October 1991), was an Italian author whose work explored family relationships, politics during and after the Fascist years and World War II, and philosophy.","title":"Natalia Ginzburg"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She wrote novels, short stories and essays, for which she received the Strega Prize and Bagutta Prize.","title":"Natalia Ginzburg"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Most of her works were also translated into English and published in the United Kingdom and United States.","title":"Natalia Ginzburg"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Elmer Glenn Cooper (9 May 1905 – 2 February 1938) was an officer in the United States Navy.","title":"Elmer Glenn Cooper"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"USS "Cooper" (DD-695), an "Allen M. Sumner"-class destroyer , is the only ship of the United States Navy to be named for Elmer Glenn Cooper, a naval aviator who died in a seaplane accident in 1938.","title":"USS Cooper"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" "Cooper" was launched 9 February 1944 by Federal Shipbuilding and Drydock Company, Kearny, New Jersey; sponsored by Mrs. Elmer G. Cooper; and commissioned 27 March 1944, Commander J. W. Schmidt in command.","title":"USS Cooper"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Giuseppe Levi (October 14, 1872 – February 3, 1965) was an Italian anatomist and histologist, professor of human anatomy (since 1916) at the universities of Sassari, Palermo and Turin.","title":"Giuseppe Levi"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was born on October 14, 1872 in Trieste to Jewish parents, Michele Levi and Emma Perugia.","title":"Giuseppe Levi"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He was married to Lidia Tanzi and had five children: Gino, Mario, Alberto, Paola (who became the wife of Adriano Olivetti), and writer Natalia Ginzburg (wife of Leone Ginzburg and mother of Carlo Ginzburg), who described her father's personality in the successful Italian book "Lessico famigliare" (1963).","title":"Giuseppe Levi"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Glenn Cooper
